# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is Firebase CLIENT config, not a secret:
# every copy of the APK contains it and it can be extracted from any downloaded binary in about
# thirty seconds (docs/mobile/phase-7-dev-loop-and-delivery.md shows how). Its API key is scoped
# to the Firebase project and restricted by package name and signing certificate.
#
# Ignoring it would mean a fresh clone builds an APK that contains firebase-messaging but none of
# the google_app_id / gcm_defaultSenderId resources it needs, so FirebaseApp never initialises,
# getExpoPushTokenAsync throws into the catch at lib/push.ts:110, and push silently does nothing
# on every device. That is the exact bug phase 7 exists to fix — do not re-introduce it here.
#
# The FCM service ACCOUNT KEY is the opposite: a real secret. It lives on EAS and never in the
# repo; the *.key / *.p8 / *.p12 / *.jks patterns above are what keep it out.

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

